{
  "$comment": "#NEW-146 (part of #NEW-143, phase 5): A THIRD-PARTY MCP SERVER'S ELICITATION REACHES THE PERSON ×4 (MCP 2026-07-28 client/elicitation). WHERE IT COMES FROM: an MCP server the agent uses asks the person something (`elicitation/create`). Codex's app-server raises it as `mcpServer/elicitation/request` (flat: the MCP request beside `serverName`, the name Exponential configured the server under) and the codex adapter maps it to THE ACP elicitation (`codex_wire::mcp_elicitation_request`), the server's name in the request's `_meta` under `serverMetaKey`, the server's property order under `orderMetaKey`; codex's private `openai/form` modes and an unreadable schema are DECLINED, never guessed at. The answer goes back as MCP's own `{action: accept|decline|cancel, content?}`. An ACP elicitation WITH `serverMetaKey` (or in url mode) is THE ELICITATION CARD below; one without it stays THE question stepper (ask-dock.json, claude's AskUserQuestion and codex's requestUserInput). THE CARD (`elicitationCard(request)`, `cardCases`, the device's: the engine builds it and posts it like every engine ask, so it is SEALED through coding mcp_gateway.rs like every other card, is a Needs you item (needs-you.json) and PUSHES (question-push.json)) = the existing `question` card with `custom: false`, `multi: false`, `question` = the server's message, a genUI `surface` built from the request and the sidecar `elicitation` {server, mode, required, url}. FORM MODE: `options` = [`copy.submit`, `copy.decline`, `copy.cancel`]; the surface = ONE vertical Stack (gap md) of ONE field per property, in the server's order (`orderMetaKey`, else by name: `elicitationFieldOrder`), each bound to `/<formKey>/<name>`: FIELD MAP: boolean = Switch (`checked`, the description as its description); a string with `enum` (labels = `enumNames` when given) or `oneOf` (labels = titles) = Select; an array (multi-select: `items.enum` or `items.anyOf`) = Select `multiple`; number = NumberField (`min`/`max`), integer = NumberField with `step` 1, `precision` 0; a string with format `date` = DatePicker; `email` = Input type email; `uri` = Input type url; any other string (`date-time` included) = Input type text. The label = the property's title, else its name; a description that is not a Switch's or a Select's rides as the placeholder. DEFAULTS ARE PREFILLED (the data model starts at each default of the right type; else `\"\"`, null for a number, false for a boolean, [] for a list). URL MODE: `options` = [`copy.done`, `copy.decline`]; the surface = the URL review (`elicitationUrl`, `urlCases`): the REGISTRABLE DOMAIN as a Heading h4 (bold; eTLD+1 with `multiPartSuffixes`, an IP or a two-label host = the host), the FULL URL as a code Text (never a link: nothing in the card is clickable but its buttons), one warning Alert per warning: `punycode` (a label starts `xn--`), `ip` (an IPv4 or IPv6 host), `insecure` (not https). A url that is not an absolute http(s) URL = `null`: the device declines it. RENDER ×4 (only existing components: the question card's AskCard chrome, its surface frame, THE Button): the header's label = the server's name (`elicitation.server`) beside `icons.server`, ALWAYS (the card names who asks); the message; the surface WITHOUT the plan card's `Preview` caption; then ONE end-aligned button row (FormActions' order): form = `copy.cancel` (ghost), `copy.decline` (outline), `copy.submit` (the small primary, disabled while `elicitationMissing(elicitation, surfaceData)` names a field, `copy.missing` under the row); url = `copy.decline` (outline), `copy.done` (outline), `copy.openLink` (the small primary). The waiting card's × (waiting-cards.json DISMISS) stays and means cancel. OPEN LINK (url mode) opens `elicitation.url` and answers NOTHING (the person comes back and presses `copy.done`): NO PREFETCH (nothing loads it before the press), never an in-app WebView: web = a new tab with `noopener,noreferrer`; desktop = the system browser; iOS = SFSafariViewController (ASWebAuthenticationSession for an OAuth URL); Android = Custom Tabs. AN ANSWER = THE answer path (`sessions.answer({messageId, answers: [label], surfaceData})`, re-sealed on the device for a sealed card); the device maps it back (`elicitationAction`, `actionCases`): `copy.submit` / `copy.done` = accept, `copy.decline` = decline, `copy.cancel`, a dismiss or anything else = cancel; NEVER AN AUTO-ACCEPT. An accepted form carries `elicitationContent(schema, surfaceData)` (`contentCases`): each value coerced to its property's type, an empty optional left out, `null` (= the card stays waiting; the renderers never send it) when a required value is missing or a value is of the wrong type or outside its choices. ANSWERED = closed like every question card: the surface inert at its answered data, the buttons gone, THE answered line names the pick. `copy.specimen` = the specimen's four captions ×4 (the waiting form, the clean url, the warned url, an answered form). Mirrors: TS src/elicitation-card.ts (the reference); the engine (eagent `engine/elicitation_card.rs`) replays `cardCases`, `contentCases`, `actionCases`, `urlCases`; the renderers (desktop `domain::elicitation_card`, iOS ExpCore `ElicitationCard.swift`, Android `domain/ElicitationCard.kt`) replay `missingCases` and `actionCases`. Whole values compared.",
